WEBVTT

00:00:00.607 --> 00:00:01.550
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.789 --> 00:00:04.590
Today, we are talking about facial massage.

00:00:05.019 --> 00:00:08.190
It is often the part of the facial that the client remembers most.

00:00:08.539 --> 00:00:11.710
But facial massage is not just rubbing to feel nice.

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.150
It is about pressure, direction, and rhythm.

00:00:15.579 --> 00:00:19.310
And most important of all, it is about knowing when not to do it.

00:00:19.993 --> 00:00:21.313
Something very common:

00:00:21.648 --> 00:00:25.448
a new therapist wants the client to see how thorough she is,

00:00:25.398 --> 00:00:29.073
so she presses really hard, drags the skin back and forth,

00:00:29.338 --> 00:00:30.993
and presses around the eyes too.

00:00:31.404 --> 00:00:34.593
The client feels pain, but is too shy to say so.

00:00:35.075 --> 00:00:39.873
The next day, the skin is red and slightly sore, and the client doesn't book again.

00:00:40.372 --> 00:00:42.913
Good facial massage is when the client can let go.

00:00:43.152 --> 00:00:46.193
If the client is still tensing up, the pressure is wrong.

00:00:46.839 --> 00:00:49.398
Before you touch the client's face, ask.

00:00:49.824 --> 00:00:55.078
If the client has a fever, a cold or the flu, or feels unwell, rebook.

00:00:55.584 --> 00:01:01.827
If the skin has a cold sore, an infection, inflamed spots with pus, broken skin,

00:01:01.777 --> 00:01:02.678
or sunburn,

00:01:02.951 --> 00:01:04.438
don't massage that area.

00:01:05.019 --> 00:01:09.520
After a recent peel, laser, cosmetic injections, or facial surgery,

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:13.638
ask whoever did the procedure how long to wait before massage.

00:01:13.884 --> 00:01:17.718
If there is an unusual lump, or a swelling with no clear reason:

00:01:17.945 --> 00:01:20.678
don't do it, and suggest the client see a doctor.

00:01:20.962 --> 00:01:22.358
We do not diagnose.

00:01:23.009 --> 00:01:25.562
If the client has an unstable condition,

00:01:25.512 --> 00:01:29.318
for example uncontrolled high blood pressure, heart disease,

00:01:29.496 --> 00:01:33.558
or treatment for a serious illness, suggest they ask their doctor first.

00:01:34.079 --> 00:01:38.577
And if the skin is red, sensitive, with small visible blood vessels,

00:01:38.527 --> 00:01:40.998
work very gently, with few movements,

00:01:41.159 --> 00:01:42.438
or skip the massage.

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:46.358
The lesson on when not to treat a client covers this in detail.

00:01:46.947 --> 00:01:52.292
The massage oil or cream must be slippery enough for your hands to glide without dragging the skin.

00:01:52.781 --> 00:01:54.452
Too little drags the skin;

00:01:54.521 --> 00:01:57.012
too much is slippery, and hard to control.

00:01:57.677 --> 00:01:59.252
Ask the client about allergies:

00:01:59.601 --> 00:02:02.292
many oils are made from nuts, like almond oil.

00:02:02.759 --> 00:02:05.572
Ask about fragrance, and essential oils, too.

00:02:06.075 --> 00:02:09.972
Use essential oils only in products the brand has already blended for the face;

00:02:10.157 --> 00:02:11.012
don't mix your own.

00:02:11.254 --> 00:02:14.692
For a sensitive client, test on a small area of skin first.

00:02:14.838 --> 00:02:18.132
Take oil with a pump, never by dipping your fingers into the bottle.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.943
Massage must suit each skin, too.

00:02:21.336 --> 00:02:23.103
Dry, dehydrated skin:

00:02:23.517 --> 00:02:27.103
use enough oil or cream, with slow, long movements.

00:02:27.442 --> 00:02:29.263
Oily or acne-prone skin:

00:02:29.532 --> 00:02:33.170
only a little oil, of a type the brand says suits oily skin,

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.503
and skip any areas with inflamed spots.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.423
Sensitive or red skin:

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:41.743
few movements, the lightest pressure, no tapping, and keep it shorter.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:43.823
Older clients with thin skin:

00:02:43.992 --> 00:02:46.863
it is even more important never to drag the skin.

00:02:47.487 --> 00:02:50.002
Facial massage has a few basic movements.

00:02:50.186 --> 00:02:51.042
Effleurage:

00:02:51.231 --> 00:02:53.682
the whole palm gliding, long and light.

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:58.242
This is the movement to open, to close, and to link the other movements.

00:02:58.569 --> 00:03:01.282
Circular kneading, a gentle petrissage:

00:03:01.551 --> 00:03:04.802
the tips of the middle and ring fingers draw small circles.

00:03:05.065 --> 00:03:06.002
Pressure holds:

00:03:06.343 --> 00:03:10.162
press slowly, hold for a few seconds, then release slowly.

00:03:10.424 --> 00:03:12.402
And light tapping, called tapotement:

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:16.162
the fingertips touching quickly and lightly, like falling rain.

00:03:16.486 --> 00:03:18.162
Skip this one on sensitive skin.

00:03:18.673 --> 00:03:20.078
Direction matters a lot.

00:03:20.463 --> 00:03:23.838
On the face, strokes usually go upward and outward:

00:03:24.187 --> 00:03:28.322
from the chin to the ears, from the sides of the nose to the temples,

00:03:28.272 --> 00:03:30.158
from the brows to the hairline.

00:03:30.722 --> 00:03:33.918
Don't drag the skin down, and don't rub back and forth.

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:35.678
Facial skin is thin;

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:39.918
drag it hard many times, and it turns red and uncomfortable.

00:03:40.089 --> 00:03:45.001
But do not promise the client that massage slims the face, or erases wrinkles,

00:03:44.951 --> 00:03:45.438
either.

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:48.958
Massage helps her relax, and the skin looks fresher;

00:03:49.139 --> 00:03:49.758
that is all.

00:03:50.376 --> 00:03:52.730
There are two areas that need the most care.

00:03:52.901 --> 00:03:53.850
The eye area:

00:03:54.036 --> 00:03:57.037
use your ring finger, because it is the weakest finger,

00:03:56.987 --> 00:03:59.290
so its pressure is naturally the lightest.

00:03:59.702 --> 00:04:02.330
Only glide along the bone around the eye socket;

00:04:02.434 --> 00:04:04.010
never press on the eyelids.

00:04:04.336 --> 00:04:05.050
The neck:

00:04:05.397 --> 00:04:09.370
only stroke lightly on the sides of the neck, moving down toward the collarbone.

00:04:09.552 --> 00:04:11.707
Do not press on the middle of the throat,

00:04:11.657 --> 00:04:14.170
and don't press deep into the sides of the neck.

00:04:14.764 --> 00:04:18.697
Pressure holds are usually done at the temples, under the cheekbones,

00:04:18.647 --> 00:04:19.934
and between the brows.

00:04:20.443 --> 00:04:22.414
Many places call them pressure points.

00:04:22.743 --> 00:04:26.974
In a spa, this is a movement for relaxation, not for treating illness.

00:04:27.546 --> 00:04:31.134
Don't promise the client it will cure headaches, or any condition at all.

00:04:31.563 --> 00:04:35.454
Press slowly, hold for a few seconds, release slowly.

00:04:35.883 --> 00:04:39.054
Press and let go suddenly, and the client will be startled.

00:04:39.731 --> 00:04:42.355
The right pressure differs from person to person.

00:04:42.753 --> 00:04:46.167
Ask the client before you start, after the first few movements,

00:04:46.117 --> 00:04:47.875
and when you move to a new area.

00:04:48.304 --> 00:04:49.155
Keep it simple:

00:04:49.533 --> 00:04:52.115
would you like it a little lighter, or a little firmer?

00:04:52.528 --> 00:04:53.475
And watch the client:

00:04:53.904 --> 00:04:59.395
a frown, holding her breath, tense shoulders, all mean the pressure is too much.

00:04:59.734 --> 00:05:02.595
A silent client is not necessarily a comfortable one.

00:05:02.833 --> 00:05:06.515
And if the client wants to lie still and not talk, respect that.

00:05:07.149 --> 00:05:10.136
The rhythm is slow, even and continuous.

00:05:10.514 --> 00:05:14.616
Once you have touched the client, always keep a hand on her when changing movements.

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:17.553
Lift both hands off and put them back suddenly,

00:05:17.503 --> 00:05:19.896
and the client loses that relaxed feeling.

00:05:20.396 --> 00:05:21.736
As for your own posture:

00:05:22.006 --> 00:05:26.658
sit on a stool at the head of the bed, adjusted to the right height, back straight,

00:05:26.608 --> 00:05:27.656
shoulders relaxed,

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:28.696
wrists straight.

00:05:28.956 --> 00:05:33.576
With many clients a day, bad posture means sore shoulders and wrists.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:36.700
Hygiene is the same as for any other service.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:39.340
Short nails, rings and watches off.

00:05:39.675 --> 00:05:42.380
Wash your hands before and after every client.

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:45.020
Towels, headbands and bed linen:

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:46.460
fresh for every client.

00:05:46.988 --> 00:05:51.340
Watch the hand hygiene lesson again, and the lesson on tools after every client.

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:57.257
If her skin turns red and stings, stop, wipe gently, apply a cool compress,

00:05:57.207 --> 00:05:58.780
and note the product,

00:05:58.874 --> 00:06:00.140
as in the incidents lesson.

00:06:00.791 --> 00:06:01.511
Finally:

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:05.191
the rules and job titles in massage differ from country to country.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:09.031
This lesson is training material, not a professional license.

00:06:09.459 --> 00:06:13.671
In the practice lesson, we will do a full facial massage, step by step.

00:06:14.021 --> 00:06:16.951
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:17.991
See you next time.
